  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the maintainer, I want a repeatable script that archives, signs and uploads a build to TestFlight, so that testers get each milestone.\n\n### Scope\n\nMac script (no `workflow_dispatch` on a non-default branch, AGENTS §11): version/build numbering above the legacy (**open question in this lot**: version and build of the first upload, which must exceed legacy 4.0.2 build 30; decided by the operator on this issue before the first upload), archive, export, upload with an App Store Connect API key kept outside the repo, release notes template. Uploading is an operator-confirmed action (AGENTS §0).\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: high · MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: MVP (#166, operator 2026-10-27): the MVP release is TestFlight only\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): legacy `push_realease.md` (release notes habit), build numbers up to 4.0.2 (30)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-161-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-080 (#98, done)\n- LOT-160 (#250)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged (unblocked 2026-10-29, steward ext/opus-helper1)\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Dry run documented; first upload done only with the operator's go, its build number recorded on the PR.\n- [ ] Version/build chosen by the operator (> 4.0.2 build 30) before the first upload; the rule for later builds written in the spec.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
